This is a ruling item for the author, as multiple choice. Every option that adds a caution needs its wording cleared under the new-message rule.

Shared predicate for (a) and (b). Do not widen R6 to amedrop > 0: lattice runs drop dose terms legitimately. Use the uz-detect P4 predicate. A treated (_i,_t) cell is hit when it has at least one dropped dose token and no live dose token at any key (any lattice bin, any contreatpoly degree). Compute it from the colnames R6 already loops over. Only if that set is nonempty, run one count over esamp & targetflag==1 & contreat != 0 to confirm the cell has rows. That count exempts empty pieces and structurally zero columns. Put it beside the R6 block, gated amelive > 0 so the two screens stay disjoint. untreatedZero never reaches it, because R5 DEF-2 already raises r(322) upstream.

(a) Void: set amevoid, amescrub and amescrublo as R6 does, and caution. Moves numbers: the ame family goes missing.

(b) Renormalize: flag the treated rows of live cells, add & flag to the subpop() of every ame margins call, and report the weight share left out. Moves numbers: the ame rises to the live-cell average. It needs about 21 call sites.

(c) Document only (the LAT L3 precedent). No code change.

Help sentence under contreat(), by option (SMCL):
(a) {it:If only some treated cohort-period cells lack within-cell dose variation, their dose slopes are not identified either. The ame results are then reported as missing in the same way.}
(b) {it:If only some treated cohort-period cells lack within-cell dose variation, their dose slopes are not identified. The ame then averages over the remaining cells only, and wooldid reports the share of weight it left out.}
(c) {it:If only some treated cohort-period cells lack within-cell dose variation, their dose slopes are dropped and enter the ame as zeros at full weight. The ame is then pulled toward zero by those cells' share of the weight. The only signal is the caution about a dropped interacted coefficient; option verbose names the cells.}

The guide's item 5 under the continuous-treatment choices (wooldid_agent_guide.md:512) takes the matching Markdown sentence.
